[E0128] Error: `yield` is a statement, not a value
   ╭─[ err/147_lend/main.wip:8:35 ]
   │
 8 │     pub fn at(index: i64): &i64 = yield self.cards.at(index)
   │                                   ──┬──
   │                                     ╰──── where a value is expected
   │
   │ Help: to lend a place from a projection, write `lend`
   │
   │ Note: `yield` is a statement that hands a value to the list being built, `own [for x in xs { yield x }]`, or to whoever asks a generator for it; in a `match` arm, it is written in braces, `{ yield x }`. A projection lends a place and stops, with `lend`
───╯
[E0419] Error: `lend` outside a projection
    ╭─[ err/147_lend/main.wip:11:39 ]
    │
 11 │ fn notAProjection(deck: &Deck): i64 = lend deck.cards.at(0)
    │                                       ──────────┬──────────
    │                                                 ╰──────────── not in a projection
    │
    │ Help: a projection declares a reference result, as in `fn heaviest(bag: &var Bag): &var Item`
────╯
